{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>your shoes.</b> He needed to say 'from your feet' because there is a shoe that is on the hand, and in the vernacular 'gant,' and it is a shoe — as was given to the redeemer, as it is written: ״איש נעלו״, and he gave it to his fellow. And even now the princes and rulers are accustomed to use their gant. And what they ask, why here he needed to remove both feet while Joshua in Jericho removed only one foot — that is because here the Shechinah preceded Moses and not him, but there Joshua preceded and acquired his place."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:34.852683251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}